{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree","id":163188,"title":"Legend of Korra season 3: Electric Jamboree","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T22:53:31-07:00","id":163188,"title":"Legend of Korra season 3: Electric Jamboree","content":"So the new Korra season is rumored to be airing fairly soon. I thought I would start the inevitable Avatar thread so we could discuss what we liked about the previous seasons as well as what we hope will happen in the next one.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm really, <i>really</i> hoping that the whole &quot;Dark avatar&quot; thing is never mentioned once in the remaining seasons. The whole thing just felt utterly ridiculous to me as a concept in the Avatar universe.<br /> <br /> I hope we get to see more spirit stuff, that was really cool. Although I hope they aren't all &quot;rawr humans bad nature good!&quot; again. That was lame.<br /> <br /> Also, less holding of the idiot ball. The series has so much potential that it has yet to live up to, I really don't want the whole thing to be a giant flop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:38:59-07:00","id":163222,"title":"","content":"The entire Korra series has been ridiculous to the Avatar Universe. If Korra had stayed about Probending and dealing with gangs we would have gotten very focused more down to earth series. It tried to be more &quot;Epic&quot; then avatar and George Lucused the fuck out of itself. I'm not really going to watch it anymore but I'm just mad about Korra in general. It had a lot of potential but it's all been wasted. Amon while a good villain is part of the issue that it had. Season 2 only made it worse. Season 3 from what I've seen hasn't changed the mold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 06-09-2014, 02:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:45:23-07:00","id":163225,"title":"","content":"And so it begins again...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/218-two-shadows","name":"Two-Shadows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar218_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T00:10:17-07:00","id":163227,"title":"","content":"Oh shit, I just now remembered this existed. I stopped watching mid-season 2, and I'm not sure I'm entirely interested in catching up.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Korra is actually a terrible series. Maybe it's just not as mind-numbingly awesome as the Last Airbender, but then again, that's a high bar. On the other hand, it's certainly not being handled well, and the fact that I just left an Avatar series mid-season with no real regrets does speak volumes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T03:12:15-07:00","id":163346,"title":"","content":"It's not exactly bad - the animation is top notch, seeing the setting progress from the original series is certainly interesting*, there are many brilliant characters, and overall I've quite enjoyed watching it.<br /> <br /> That said, as a sequel to this near-perfect thing Avatar: the Last Airbender was, it fails. Miserably. It started off pretty good, with a naive, hot-headed protagonist facing a social issue that couldn't be either talked down easily or punched in the face until it went away, but then it all went downhill. First season had a decent story, but felt rushed, especially in it's conclusion - I really think it needed a few more episodes to wrap things up, and I'd much rather they left the issue of Korra losing her bending for season two (though I understand that wasn't on the table as they needed to wrap everything up in case the series got discontinued - still, executive meddling may explain missed potential, but not excuse it).<br /> <br /> Then, season two pretty much abandoned all nuance in an effort to crank things up to eleven, and it sucked. They turned probably the subtlest, most morally ambiguous setting in the history of children television into yet another good versus evil cliche with a Stupid Evil villain whose grand plan would make Skeletor cringe. The season still had it's moments - for all my misgivings about the changes to the mythology of the setting, the story of the First Avatar had a gorgeous style, a powerful setting and a great, likable protagonist, and I couldn't help but feel warm when Korra met Uncle Iroh in the spirit world - but as a whole, it was weak, forced, and contrary to the first season, seemed horribly dragged.<br /> <br /> I'll still watch the third season, mostly in hopes of seeing more Tenzin (or, as my friends and I call him, Kejak's nicer brother) and several other characters I've grown fond of, and on the off-chance they'll get their shit together and finally give us something worthy of it's great predecessor, but I'm not holding my breath.<br /> <br /> *I usually don't give such issues much thought, but writing this rant I realized the &quot;updated&quot; setting feels a bit... whitewashed? It's not like they neglected the ethnic diversity of the original, but compared to this awesomely exotic world straight out of Asian myths that was given to us in the original series, it's like they tried to downplay the exotic and ethnically diverse aspects by burying them under as many trappings of a modern western civilization as possible. It's not a major problem for me, and it's not like I don't like the new setting (and I greatly appreciate the amount of thought they've put into blending magic and technology in an internally consistent way, rather than just handwaving the whole industrial revolution entirely), but I think in a way it feels more standard by the inclusion of all the technology, something you'd expect to see in a Saturday morning cartoon, and not quite as alien (and thus interesting) as the setting of the original.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T03:44:06-07:00","id":163359,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163346#post163346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*I usually don't give such issues much thought, but writing this rant I realized the &quot;updated&quot; setting feels a bit... whitewashed? It's not like they neglected the ethnic diversity of the original, but compared to this awesomely exotic world straight out of Asian myths that was given to us in the original series, it's like they tried to downplay the exotic and ethnically diverse aspects by burying them under as many trappings of a modern western civilization as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welcome to early 20th century Shanghai.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:01:18-07:00","id":163593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163346#post163346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The season still had it's moments - for all my misgivings about the changes to the mythology of the setting, the story of the First Avatar had a gorgeous style, a powerful setting and a great, likable protagonist, and I couldn't help but feel warm when Korra met Uncle Iroh in the spirit world - but as a whole, it was weak, forced, and contrary to the first season, seemed horribly dragged.</div> </div> </div> </div>The tragic part is that Wan basically had more growth and development in the two episodes he appeared in than Korra did throughout two seasons. He started out as a petty thief and survivor, and grew into the first Avatar, the saviour of humanity and bridge between worlds. Korra? She started out as a rash, stubborn kid whose only solution to problems is to punch them and ended up the exact same way. She also decided to go through with a plan concocted by a lunatic, but had not stopped for five seconds to think about where the Equalists are coming from. The merging of the worlds, incidentally, basically screws over non-benders something fierce - as Bumi's oh-so-hilarious stumbling around showed, they're utterly powerless against spirits. So they're going to be entirely reliant on benders for protection against spirits who misbehave. Good going, Korra. I'm sure the surviving Equalists appreciate being proven right about you.<br /> <br /> I'm probably going to watch Season Three, but it'll be due to my morbid curiosity that I can't suppress. The first season of Korra was a massive disappointment and the second one followed up on that. I've honestly begun to think the success of Last Airbender was mostly an accident. Or maybe the writers just can't handle subtlety - TLA took one of the most basic, well-worn premises in the history of fiction and made it good. Then they tried to introduce more complex issues in Season One of Korra, and planted their faces in the mud while doing it. They created a brilliant antagonist in Amon, and then they proceeded to ruin them within a half hour of exposition - from a mysterious, charismatic terrorist mastermind who scares the Avatar herself witless despite being a non-bender, he turned into a bloodbender with daddy issues, incoherent motivation and implausible powers, who was ultimately defeated through a combination of an inexplicable bout of stupidity and dumb luck.<br /> <br /> Then again, Season Two had no subtlety whatsoever and yet it failed as well. So who knows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":186,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","user":"Morty","date":". 06-09-2014, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:27:27-07:00","id":163612,"title":"","content":"If you can steel yourself, I highly recommend not watching the season until it's complete. Not that it necessarily improves anything, but you save yourself a lot of mental hassle that comes with concocting potential future scenarios the real show can't live up to. Just 1.5X through the talky scenes, savor the fights, and then go back and read the forum discussions where people gave the writers way too much as they tried to extrapolate hypothetical plots. <br /> <br /> The ongoing &quot;Varrick is the Big Bad and will be important!!&quot; arguments were particularly amusing after a binge intake of the season.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Good going, Korra. I'm sure the surviving Equalists appreciate being proven right about you. </div> </div> </div>This requires the show actually acknowledging the Equalists ever again [sadtrombone.gif].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T08:53:00-07:00","id":163625,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to note what depths people see in <a href=\"http://crystalzelda.tumblr.com/post/84232512740/why-was-korra-hated-for-rightfully-chewing-out-tenzin\" target=\"_blank\">Korra's character arc.</a> I mostly view it as wasted potential (I view a lot of things in the Legend of Korra as sadly wasted potential; oh, that first season had such <i>promise</i>), but it's interesting nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:17:46-07:00","id":163659,"title":"","content":"I just wanted Kung-fu Hustle Avatar, was that so much to ask?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:25:31-07:00","id":163672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163612#post163612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This requires the show actually acknowledging the Equalists ever again [sadtrombone.gif].</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, if I screwed up that badly as a writer, I'd want to forget it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:02:05-07:00","id":163718,"title":"","content":"Now would probably be as appropriate a time as any to post the comic I drew immediately after seeing the Season 2 finale.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s23.postimg.org/3mnvt5v6z/Korra_Abridged.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:15:22-07:00","id":163755,"title":"","content":"I've avoided all Korra threads wherever I'm at. The reason is that I keep reading &quot;m\u00f1e the show's not cool as Aang's m\u00f1eee&quot;... And although I respect that anyone can have his own opinion, I can't help but feel like people are unfair with the things they like. This begs the question &quot;why did you like it in the first place only to start hating it later?&quot;, and many would blame the creators: &quot;this or that didn't make sense&quot; &quot;the previous show didn't do this or that&quot; &quot;X was lame&quot; etc...<br /> <br /> And you know, being a creator is hard, The Legend of Aang wasn't perfect, but it was a GREAT show, and I as part of the audience have chosen to focus on the things I like, and if you ask me what I think about Avatar (both Legend of Aang and Korra) I'll say &quot;It is a great show, and I feel like the creators really have their hearts on the story they want to tell, and really gave life to the characters they wanted us to know&quot;. I don't give a damn if a certain nerd on the internet rages because of the lion turtle or Zukko's mom or whatever.<br /> <br /> But you know... being part of the audience is hard too. You can either simply sit in front of the TV and say &quot;this is bullshit&quot; or you can remember why you decided to sit, you wanted to get into little worlds not your own maybe. You decided to witness whatever happens for a couple of hours. And sudenly people like Avatar, and for whatever reason feel like they have the absolute right to &quot;know&quot; how it should have been done. I'm sorry, but the story is still a creation of the creators. The audience tends to get corrosive about things that should make them happy. They're still making the show! We can still see this type of characters! The animation and action sequences are of the best quality! There aren't many shows like Avatar. And everything people dislike isn't enough to objectively say &quot;The show is crap&quot;.<br /> <br /> Remember the Street Fighter movie? THAT WAS CRAP. And nowadays people talk about it and even watch it with a lighter mood, and say &quot;this crap is so awesomely crap!&quot;. What's wrong with us? Why can we enjoy goofy shit just because it is nostalgic, while the good stuff &quot;isn't good enough for our finest tastes&quot;?<br /> <br /> And last... Say what you will about the Legend of Korra, but in a world in which cheap ass creators are terrified to push stories further, a world in which every now and then we get PREQUELS or MIDQUELS, we have to admit the Legend of Korra has balls to show us the world beyond Legend of Aang. Not many creators have the courage and talent to do so. I applaud their decision and enjoy the story they show me, not the one I &quot;think I could have done better&quot;. <br /> <br /> I hope nobody gets mad at me, these were just my two cents and I'll be leaving this topic in 3, 2, 1...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:22:59-07:00","id":163783,"title":"","content":"I have a sneaking suspicion that I'm the only one that thought season 2 was better than season 1.<br /> <br /> Season 1 had too much going on and didn't really focus on anything. Not enough time was given to Korra's development as a person, not enough time was given to the Equalists for them to become credible, the thing with the city's criminal gangs almost got glossed over entirely... I get the impression that the authors weren't all on board with each other about how the whole season would play out, or maybe they had gotten used to having multiple seasons to spend faffing around. The Last Airbender was good, but it had a LOT of airtime to develop things gradually, and it used a fair amount of filler.<br /> <br /> Season 2 was more coherent. There was one major plot that got introduced in the first episode that got almost exclusive focus for every following episode. All of the sideplots were clearly tied to the main one. I can't really think of anything that I feel didn't get enough explanation or could have been given more development time.<br /> <br /> Also, I would like to state my belief that the Avatar fandom is utterly insane. They're right up there with the MLP and the Portal 2 lunatics who invest <i>so much mental energy</i> into interpreting and understanding and sharing what they feel about what is, at the end of the day, a cartoon intended for light entertainment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":"is easily misconstrued 06-09-2014, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:33:43-07:00","id":163796,"title":"","content":"I often feel the same, Gonzo. I generally try to be positive, to focus on what things do well, and I think there's a lot to love in the first two seasons of Legend of Korra. Many characters were great, and the show has a lot of exciting and moving moments leading up to the finales.<br /> <br /> It's just... nothing bugs me quite like missed potential and stumbling climaxes. Where I felt The Last Airbender took a while to get going, Legend of Korra was excellent up until the ending, where it stumbled and fell. And... I much prefer the former. The Last Airbender's ending wasn't quite what I was hoping for either, but not to that level.<br /> <br /> Still, I'm going to watch the third season, and hope that this time it reaches a conclusion I find satisfying. And even if it doesn't... I'll still have a lot of fun on the way there, I'm sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/157-phoenix_kensai","name":"Phoenix_Kensai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar157_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T10:45:25-07:00","id":163803,"title":"","content":"I'm not honestly sure that I could choose between season one and two. They both had different failings. Season two captured the globetrotting feel and had less Sportland Sports, but regressing Korra's character and repeating the love triangle just made it worse the second time around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:07:49-07:00","id":163810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's interesting to note what depths people see in <a href=\"http://crystalzelda.tumblr.com/post/84232512740/why-was-korra-hated-for-rightfully-chewing-out-tenzin\" target=\"_blank\">Korra's character arc.</a> I mostly view it as wasted potential (I view a lot of things in the Legend of Korra as sadly wasted potential; oh, that first season had such <i>promise</i>), but it's interesting nonetheless. </div> </div> </div>There's a scene in Korra Season 2 where Aang's three kids are doing something and the writing very quickly sketches out that the two bending siblings have a connection not shared by the non-bender, and the two non-Aang faves have a connection not shared by Tenzin, and that these bonds probably run very deep and inform a lot of their interactions. Then nothing is ever done to capitalize on this.<br /> <br /> It was then that I realized their writer's room white board prolly looks all &quot;1. Introduce Interesting Elements 2. ??? 3. Narrative Satisfaction!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> at the end of the day, a cartoon aimed at teenagers. </div> </div> </div>Don't do that. Please. Target audience sets some limits on allowable content, but has nothing to do with allowable quality.<br /> <br /> I mean, yeesh, it's sentiments like that which lead to the continuing dreck of &quot;You should feel embarrassed for enjoying [YA/Comics/Cartoons/Genre-Fiction/RPGs/etc.]&quot; articles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:15:22-07:00","id":163818,"title":"","content":"In the end, the Big Problems (TM) with Season One and Season Two come down to one word: Pacing.<br /> <br /> In Season One, this was a result of the sudden expansion of Korra from a miniseries to a full-blown saga, with things feeling simultaneously rushed and protracted in places. The worst example, of course, was the last two minutes of the first season, which managed to utterly unmake all the character development Korra had over the rest of the season.<br /> <br /> In Season Two, this was an example of the creators not seeming to know where they wanted to go. At one moment we might be following Tarrlok and his GREAT IDEAS about spirits (and boy did his character swallow the villain ball in the second half of the season), then the wackiness of Varrick would show up, and then <i>it's time for a serious police investigation</i>, before we wrap up with that fucking love triangle. It took half the season (and the story of Wan) for things to finally kick into gear, but by then Korra had lost a lot of its fans.<br /> <br /> However... I still think it's a good series. Korra's fun to watch when she's not an idiot, Mako and Bolin got some decent character development, I'm really excited to see what Asami does, Desna and Eska are wonderfully deadpan, and every scene with Varrick is still joyous. The fights are still top notch, Amon is a genuinely terrifying villain (and his backstory was a lot easier to swallow on a second viewing), I loved the stuff with Tenzin and his family, and pro-bending is still awesome <i>and I will fight anyone with knives who says otherwise.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:31:43-07:00","id":163830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> pro-bending is still awesome <i>and I will fight anyone with knives who says otherwise.</i> </div> </div> </div><br /> In lieu of knives...maybe explain the appeal? Like, if I'm the budget guy and I say we have enough animation bux for X scenes of pro-bending or X scenes of general bending combat, why might I be persuaded to allocate money to the pro-bending side?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/870-side-item","name":"Side Item","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar870_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T11:32:05-07:00","id":163831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163810#post163810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't do that. Please. Target audience sets some limits on allowable content, but has nothing to do with allowable quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, I could probably have phrased that better.<br /> <br /> What I meant to say is that the point of the show is to provide light entertainment. It's not there to educate you or influence your philosophical outlook, although it might do both of those things. I think it's unrealistic to demand a great deal of depth from something that isn't really meant to make you think hard about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:22:31-07:00","id":163890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163755#post163755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And last... Say what you will about the Legend of Korra, but in a world in which cheap ass creators are terrified to push stories further, a world in which every now and then we get PREQUELS or MIDQUELS, we have to admit the Legend of Korra has balls to show us the world beyond Legend of Aang. Not many creators have the courage and talent to do so. I applaud their decision and enjoy the story they show me, not the one I &quot;think I could have done better&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you're saying, and it's why I was hugely enthusiastic about LoK... right until the Season One finale. But there are things I just can't forgive. Simple as that. I'd also like to kindly ask people to stop implying that those who criticize LoK do so because of comparing it to TLA. Maybe some do, but <i>I</i> don't. I judge it on its own merits, and they're lacking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163818#post163818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Season Two, this was an example of the creators not seeming to know where they wanted to go. At one moment we might be following Tarrlok and his GREAT IDEAS about spirits (and boy did his character swallow the villain ball in the second half of the season), then the wackiness of Varrick would show up, and then <i>it's time for a serious police investigation</i>, before we wrap up with that fucking love triangle. It took half the season (and the story of Wan) for things to finally kick into gear, but by then Korra had lost a lot of its fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unalok, not Tarrlok. Tarrlok was from Season One. Not that I blame you, since those guys are kind of interchangeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T12:34:57-07:00","id":163900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163718#post163718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now would probably be as appropriate a time as any to post the comic I drew immediately after seeing the Season 2 finale.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://s23.postimg.org/3mnvt5v6z/Korra_Abridged.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>It'll quench you. It's the quenchiest!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:20:18-07:00","id":163946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Side Item</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163830#post163830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/I] In lieu of knives...maybe explain the appeal? Like, if I'm the budget guy and I say we have enough animation bux for X scenes of pro-bending or X scenes of general bending combat, why might I be persuaded to allocate money to the pro-bending side?</div> </div> </div> </div> One of the things the Avatar series has been good about has been showing how bending can be used in non-combat, utilitarian ways: earthbending and waterbending are used to travel quickly across the ground or sea, firebending is used to forge metal, lightningbending is used to power electronics, and so on. It goes a long way to flesh out the world, and show how bending affects society as a whole, rather than just being a bunch of flashy fighting techniques.<br /> <br /> But one thing that was often missing was entertainment and leisure, and something like the pro-bending league makes a lot of sense in the newly industrialized world of Avatar, sort of an extension of the earthbender wrestling league from the first series. It's also an interesting way to show off bending in a highly controlled scenario, where the characters have to come up with new and interesting ways to fight within the constraints of the rules. Now, there is a caveat to this: pro-bending is best as a &quot;sometimes&quot; food, so to speak. Too much, and it will get boring, but I see no reason not to give us the occasional pro-bending match to add variety to the various fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":283,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","user":"MrInsecure","date":". 06-09-2014, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:22:31-07:00","id":163951,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the wall of text, posting from my phone. Will edit later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T13:27:30-07:00","id":163954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163946#post163946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One of the things the Avatar series has been good about has been showing how bending can be used in non-combat, utilitarian ways: earthbending and waterbending are used to travel quickly across the ground or sea, firebending is used to forge metal, lightningbending is used to power electronics, and so on. It goes a long way to flesh out the world, and show how bending affects society as a whole, rather than just being a bunch of flashy fighting techniques. But one thing that was often missing was entertainment and leisure, and something like the pro-bending league makes a lot of sense in the newly industrialized world of Avatar, sort of an extension of the earthbender wrestling league from the first series. It's also an interesting way to show off bending in a highly controlled scenario, where the characters have to come up with new and interesting ways to fight within the constraints of the rules. Now, there is a caveat to this: pro-bending is best as a &quot;sometimes&quot; food, so to speak. Too much, and it will get boring, but I see no reason not to give us the occasional pro-bending match to add variety to the various fights.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If it had been done better, pro-bending could have been a great conduit for Korra's character development. It started out this way - instead of brute-forcing her way through the opposition, which was her first instinct, she had to use tactics and play within the rules. Unfortunately, nothing came of it, in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T14:58:26-07:00","id":164065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163954#post163954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed. If it had been done better, pro-bending could have been a great conduit for Korra's character development. It started out this way - instead of brute-forcing her way through the opposition, which was her first instinct, she had to use tactics and play within the rules. Unfortunately, nothing came of it, in the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>They just never had enough time in the first season.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:15:10-07:00","id":164082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=164065#post164065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They just never had enough time in the first season.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you... are you saying there wasn't enough pro bending?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T15:35:33-07:00","id":164096,"title":"","content":"You know what? Yeah, I'd have liked to have seen more pro-bending. As in, I would have liked for there to be more time to explore Korra's growth through doing something vaguely normal, I'd have liked for there to be time to mix up the way the matches worked so the benders could cut loose, like a match on a stone platform where earthbenders were forbidden to attack and are instead tasked with building and repairing a fortress to protect their teammates. I'd have liked more time to explore the background and implications of the sport.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem, I think, is that any time pro bending turned up, it was &quot;welp, time for a match now now now&quot; with maybe a little pre-match dialogue. Too often it was really just an excuse to fit an action scene in, and it could've been more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are no problems, only plothooks.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1P2AuLM6D1Et9mWQVJp-ugWujFJhTi2VwQBtOazOW1Mg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Terrifying Argent Witches Hub</a><br /> <i>Originally posted by </i><b><i>Dex Davican</i></b><br /> I need them for my collection: <i>Enormous Gonads of 2012: A Retrospective.</i>","edited":{"userid":920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","user":"Imrix","date":". 06-09-2014, 06:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/920-imrix","name":"Imrix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T16:05:03-07:00","id":164173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=164082#post164082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you... are you saying there wasn't enough pro bending?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Imrix got most of it already, but I'd like to add a few things. Pro-bending was something that let the show put in some action scenes without needing to have kung-fu assassins always attacking the Avatar. It could have given them a small tournament arc if the matches had been better detailed so that they could show some actual struggle like a good sports movie. It could have given them a vehicle to develop some good character traits in Korra and could have let them move the Korra/Mako/Asami love triangle along more naturally through some teammate bonding.<br /> <br /> Pro-bending is so derided only because we didn't get to explore it's potential because the plot had to run in half the time it should have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T18:37:36-07:00","id":164281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imrix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=164096#post164096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what? Yeah, I'd have liked to have seen more pro-bending. As in, I would have liked for there to be more time to explore Korra's growth through doing something vaguely normal, I'd have liked for there to be time to mix up the way the matches worked so the benders could cut loose, like a match on a stone platform where earthbenders were forbidden to attack and are instead tasked with building and repairing a fortress to protect their teammates. I'd have liked more time to explore the background and implications of the sport.<br /> <br /> Part of the problem, I think, is that any time pro bending turned up, it was &quot;welp, time for a match now now now&quot; with maybe a little pre-match dialogue. Too often it was really just an excuse to fit an action scene in, and it could've been more than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure. If The Great Divide was some deep insight into the nature of the Avatar's wisdom and a development of Aang's character, I'm sure it would be remembered as a classic. If it were <i>good</i>, it would be <i>good</i>. I'm not sure time is the issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=164173#post164173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Imrix got most of it already, but I'd like to add a few things. Pro-bending was something that let the show put in some action scenes without needing to have kung-fu assassins always attacking the Avatar. It could have given them a small tournament arc if the matches had been better detailed so that they could show some actual struggle like a good sports movie. It could have given them a vehicle to develop some good character traits in Korra and could have let them move the Korra/Mako/Asami love triangle along more naturally through some teammate bonding.<br /> <br /> Pro-bending is so derided only because we didn't get to explore it's potential because the plot had to run in half the time it should have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sceptical. Tournament arcs in shows always feel like boring filler to me, and this one was running on the tortuous side already. If there were any more, regardless of underdog-sports-movie framing, I don't think I could have even finished it.<br /> <br /> And really, now more time for the <i>love triangle</i>. I'm not sure we can agree on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 06-10-2014, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:14:10-07:00","id":164300,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the existence of pro-bending as a thing that exists in the setting. It is a good parallel to Martial Arts going from survival/killing to sport. That said, I'd have vastly, <i>immensely</i> preferred if it was just a background detail, like showing firebenders being employed to generate electricity <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(which was also neat, but I certainly would not want multiple episodes dedicated entirely to it) </span>.<br /> <br /> But pro-bending as a huge thing, with the main characters getting involved in a major tournament and basically entire episodes dedicated to matches in a Season that, among its problems, suffered from having too few episodes to tell its story appropriately? To hell with that.<br /> <br /> The Deus Ex Arbor in the end of season two was the worst thing in the series for me, though. And season two as a whole, while it had its moments, was largely disappointing. Oh, well. At least the comedy and the fighting scenes were still good. I'll probably end up watching season 3 eventually, if only for the jokes and combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T03:58:12-07:00","id":164696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=164281#post164281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sure. If The Great Divide was some deep insight into the nature of the Avatar's wisdom and a development of Aang's character, I'm sure it would be remembered as a classic. If it were <i>good</i>, it would be <i>good</i>. I'm not sure time is the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, though. The Great Divide was an irrelevant, clich\u00e9d distraction and that's that. But pro-bending <i>could</i> have been good, perhaps, if it had been given enough time. Korra was powerful from the start of the show, but had trouble thinking and acting in terms other than punching through obstacles with her bending. Having to play by the rules, as part of a team and with a goal other than just smacking the opposition aside with her power was a challenge to her character - at first. It never got anywhere, and that's the problem. People deride pro-bending because it took up time in a season that was rushed and badly paced, but it was not without potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T10:16:29-07:00","id":164916,"title":"","content":"I think <i>The Legend of Korra</i> is the first show I've seen to suffer in its quality because of a LACK of filler, rather than an abundance of it. If Season One had had even a few more episodes to devote to exploring various characters and their relationships, the whole plot might have felt more natural, more <i>complete</i>. Maybe we could have seen Korra go undercover, disguised as a non-bender, and meet a cell of genuinely heroic Equalists who are protecting non-benders from the triads like she did when she first arrived in the city. Maybe we could have seen flashbacks showing how Naga and Korra first met.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how Season Two could have been salvaged, but if the writers had been given more than twelve episodes they might have had a chance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T10:54:01-07:00","id":164952,"title":"","content":"Season 1 of Korra was pretty disappointing. It started off really well and just imploded in the last couple of episodes.<br /> <br /> I dropped Season 2 about halfway through and have no interest in watching Season 3. Which is a shame, because Avatar was a great series - I've watched it 3 times now. And I actually like Korra a lot as a character. I just think they've done a really poor job handling her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T15:16:22-07:00","id":167265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163783#post163783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a sneaking suspicion that I'm the only one that thought season 2 was better than season 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved it. More than season 1 (loved season 1 too).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T17:05:36-07:00","id":178431,"title":"","content":"So apparently, Nickelodeon announced that the next season is starting this Friday while I wasn't paying attention: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A0UBbzeFc74\" data-code=\"A0UBbzeFc74\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/A0UBbzeFc74/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> And hey, it looks like there's going to be some actual continuity with the events of the second season! I'm really hoping this is a sign that the staff were able to nail down a coherent story this time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-23T21:45:13-07:00","id":178639,"title":"","content":"Considering how abrupt the time was and the Deathslot it's getting. I doubt they think it'll succeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-25T19:07:58-07:00","id":180266,"title":"","content":"whatever we think about the previous seasons, at least we can all agree that Mako is barely a human being","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T12:42:57-07:00","id":183156,"title":"","content":"Korra and Asami have much better chemistry with each other than they do with Mako.<br /> Just saying...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T23:07:17-07:00","id":183550,"title":"","content":"I love that elevator conversation Zuko had with the twins.<br /> <br /> I'm getting major Aang vibes from Kai for some reason, despite them being quite different.<br /> <br /> And it's very fun seeing the Dai Li again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T03:31:11-07:00","id":183677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=183156#post183156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Korra and Asami have much better chemistry with each other than they do with Mako.<br /> Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>It really is weird to see any actual chemistry between Team Avatar. Where was it in the first season?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T06:44:57-07:00","id":184761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=183677#post183677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It really is weird to see any actual chemistry between Team Avatar. Where was it in the first season?</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Korra and Asami there were glimpses of it but there was the love triangle with Mako and the subtle teasing that Asami might be an Equalist got in the way of it.<br /> <br /> I think Mako is basically Bruce Wayne if he had to raise a younger brother rather than having Alfred as a father substitute. He's got the quiet anger down because aside from his family, being a cop seems to be the only thing that's really held his interest.<br /> <br /> The downside of this is that Bruce Wayne is often considered a shell for his other persona.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T10:27:23-07:00","id":184940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=184761#post184761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Korra and Asami there were glimpses of it but there was the love triangle with Mako and the subtle teasing that Asami might be an Equalist got in the way of it.<br /> <br /> I think Mako is basically Bruce Wayne if he had to raise a younger brother rather than having Alfred as a father substitute. He's got the quiet anger down because aside from his family, being a cop seems to be the only thing that's really held his interest.<br /> <br /> The downside of this is that Bruce Wayne is often considered a shell for his other persona.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with a lot of other elements in the first season, there just wasn't enough time to develop the relations between them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T12:23:38-07:00","id":184991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrInsecure</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=163818#post163818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, the Big Problems (TM) with Season One and Season Two come down to one word: Pacing.<br /> <br /> In Season One, this was a result of the sudden expansion of Korra from a miniseries to a full-blown saga, with things feeling simultaneously rushed and protracted in places. The worst example, of course, was the last two minutes of the first season, which managed to utterly unmake all the character development Korra had over the rest of the season.<br /> <br /> In Season Two, this was an example of the creators not seeming to know where they wanted to go. At one moment we might be following Tarrlok and his GREAT IDEAS about spirits (and boy did his character swallow the villain ball in the second half of the season), then the wackiness of Varrick would show up, and then <i>it's time for a serious police investigation</i>, before we wrap up with that fucking love triangle. It took half the season (and the story of Wan) for things to finally kick into gear, but by then Korra had lost a lot of its fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> The first season of Korra suffered <i>heavily</i> from being only a single season that was intended to be a self-contained story. There's a lot of things that could have been explored: the Evil Empire of the Fire Nation got more fleshing out than the Equalists did--I honestly think Pema's disappointment at being told her next child would be a bender was at least conceived with the idea of hooking into something greater in the narrative, or at least touching on the alienation and powerlessness it's possible to feel when you're surrounded by people who are special in a way you can never be--and I have yet to speak to anyone who feels Korra's restoration at the end of the story was a good move. Season two...well, hey. I actually liked it quite a bit, ridiculous power escalation be damned. Maybe it's because I only recently watched the second half of that season yesterday, after watching up through the history of Wan long enough ago for everything else to kind of slip away. Under other circumstances I would be miffed at the restoration of Rava, but that seed was explicitly sown several episodes earlier, well before it became relevant.<br /> <br /> Frankly, Avatar's pacing has always been its weak point for me. There have been episodes and plotlines even throughout Aang's tale that just didn't flow well. The lessons of Guru Pathik bugged the crap out of me: (Aang: &quot;[Established character baggage].&quot; Pathik: &quot;[Platitude].&quot; Aang: &quot;Okay. Next!&quot;) and I feel that as much as there are people who insist that the images of the Lion-Turtle earlier in the story were sufficient foreshadowing for the payoff in the final episodes, I strongly, strongly, STRONGLY feel that the whole thing would have been made much better--and gone down smoother--if we'd gotten its koan or riddle or whatever significantly earlier in the season. Aang's refusal to kill is a fine character trait, and I'm pretty sure it's established early on--I know at least as early as Bato of the Water Tribe we know he's a strict vegetarian--but as much as that defines the final episodes of his series, it seems to only come up occasionally: I'm not the first or the last to point out that the climbing tanks of the Northern Air Temple that were cut from their cables and plummeted to the ground probably didn't land with their contents intact. While the struggle between needing a way to deal with Ozai <i>now</i> and cleaving to one's strict ethical beliefs is a fine story, the way the final four episodes are structured--and the way they were aired--made it the Problem Of The Episode, to be brought up then cleanly and quickly resolved in a single narrative swipe.<br /> <br /> Ghhh.<br /> <br /> Okay, stopping my rant now. I am seriously and honestly looking forward to actually getting to watch this next book of Korra stories, but I may have to wait a while for it. u_u;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T16:08:23-07:00","id":185186,"title":"","content":"So... anyone have any speculation on why the four imprisoned benders are interested in killing the Avatar?<br /> <br /> Heck, I have a neat theory on why the Earth Queen should be up for that. 'Cause killing Korra will cause an earth-nation Avatar to be born and if she plays her cards right, that new Avatar might be Earth Nationalist and all for reclaiming Republic City and the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> Doesn't seem like the Quartet of Evil Benders (or QEB) would be up for that though. That sounds more like Dai Li secret plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/746-kunoichi","name":"Kunoichi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar746_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T16:14:16-07:00","id":185192,"title":"","content":"Well... you know... trying to kill the Avatar happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-02T11:28:08-07:00","id":186433,"title":"","content":"So far I really like how tightly together they've kept things. You have two major plots (find the airbenders/four crazy element people) and they seem to be focusing on those very well. New characters (like the thief kid) are introduced to help enforce those plots, which I like. They don't seem to be going all over the place (yet) and so far I'm willing to give it another go.<br /> <br /> Also, the conversation between Zuko and the Twins during the elevator ride down was hilarious. Loved it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T13:38:02-07:00","id":195719,"title":"","content":"Now that we are 5 episodes in, I gotta say I consider this season so far a considerable improvement over many of the mistakes of the last two. Now it is waiting and seeing if pissing off a queen will have further consequences and if the motives of the four main villains will not be stupid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T14:13:40-07:00","id":195737,"title":"","content":"Thoughts during the new episode:<br /> <br /> I love the idea of a metal bender city.<br /> <br /> &quot;new airbender&quot; huh? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Toph got a statue, and apparently she's alive. I hope we get to see her.<br /> <br /> Opal, huh? Interesting name. Seems like a nice character.<br /> <br /> &quot;Be the leaf!&quot; Ominous training is ominous.<br /> <br /> Bolin is making moves, lots of moves.<br /> <br /> Holy shit Verrick! Awesome!<br /> <br /> I like seeing Lin's backstory.<br /> <br /> Air Bender vs Water Bender! Fight!<br /> <br /> Aw Lin <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Overall, I'm still cautiously optimistic about the new season, but it really does seem to be progressing well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T15:27:33-07:00","id":195796,"title":"","content":"\u200bI haven't been able to watch a single episode of this season. Normally I would catch full episodes at Nick.com/Korra, but they've only been airing clips from the episodes... and we're already approaching the 10 episode mark. Even Hulu isn't helpful as it sends you to the Nick.com page. Which is totally great if I want to watch clips and not FULL FREAKING EPISODES! *flips tables* I've tried watching videos uploaded onto Youtube, but they're either in a language that I'm not fluent in, of poor quality or off-centered viewing ratio. &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> I can empathize with the people who are unimpressed with the entire Korra series. Often times I find myself being the only person in the crowd that actually likes. I'm not saying it's great, or even as inspiring as the Last Airbender, but I like it none-the-less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>First Age Spray may cause temporary insanity, limit breaks or usurptions. Do not use First Age Spray on children. If Shogunate persists, please see your doctor. - Megapope<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://farm4.staticflickr.com/3923/14658615863_c919f4c13c_s.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1099-noshpan","name":"noshpan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1099_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T16:53:18-07:00","id":195831,"title":"","content":"By far the best season, and I enjoyed the last two. They've finally found their footing with the shorter format I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T20:36:36-07:00","id":195967,"title":"","content":"On another note, I like the whole &quot;Spirit bending&quot; that Jenor is doing now that she's not playing the role of &quot;The Chosen One.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T05:32:16-07:00","id":196203,"title":"","content":"I kind of noticed that each season of LoK tries to do something different in relation to The Last Airbender, with the Air trying to scale it down again, because they thought it'd be hard topping the finale of Last Airbender, and instead focused on a single city instead of the entire world, with an enemy force that steadily got stronger. Outside of the dumb lovetriangle, I liked it.<br /> Spirits tried to outdo the first part of Avatar, making the villains bigger and the stakes higher, with the faith of two worlds in their hands instead of one, being more over the top, needless to say, it didn't really work, at least, not for me.<br /> Change, so far, seems to go back to the way The Last Airbender was, a group of colorful characters, travelling the world, with individual episodes that focus on smaller things, which are slowly building up on top of eachother to something big. Zaheer seems like a way more interesting villain than the guy we had in the last season (I forgot his name already), he has kind of a warrior-poet thing going on, and while I have no idea what his plans are, I am interested in what he's planning. At the very least he isn't telling what he's planning to do right at the start of the season.<br /> <br /> Also, Major Spoiler/Rant about Spirits, if you have not seen it, do not open this, it literally spoils the last two episodes.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">A DARK AVATAR?! WHAT THE FUCK IS WRONG WITH YOU PEOPLE!</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T20:19:45-07:00","id":203412,"title":"","content":"Good to see Toph again. From the what we already knew I suspected she wouldn't be all that great as a mom, so no surprises there. Also, baby air bisons are really cute.<br /> <br /> This season continues to be much better than the first two, in my opinion. It even feels like Korra has learned and matured a bit. Though If I am to nitpick, I hope Tenzin manages to become a better teacher by the end. His children are all excellent airbenders, especially for their age, but he pretty much sucked at teaching Korra and these new airbenders.<br /> <br /> Now, if I remember correctly about the season length, we are already about halfway through. This makes me a little worried that the last few episodes might feel a somewhat too rushed considering that one of the main plot lines, about those 4 criminals, has not being developed that much yet. I wonder if they'll be dealt with in this season or continue to be the antagonists for the next one.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: also, a bit more Asami, please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T17:20:58-07:00","id":205452,"title":"","content":"I actually don't have any problems with Korra(and, God help me and my tasteless, tacky soul, I don't have any problems with Season 2's [SPOILERS!!]). So far this season is awesome, though the Earth Queen makes me mad. Turning the Earth Kingdom into North Korea and EATING her father's bear? Not cool. Zaheer is, I admit, a much better &quot;spiritual&quot; villain than Unloqk(I can't really spell his name), and his, for lack of an official name, Irregulars are all awesome. I feel bad for Lin, and I actually find myself on her side as of the most recent episode. Comparing their actions and how their lives are now(not saying exactly what in case they're considered spoilers), she has the right to feel just a little miffed. I'm the &quot;good&quot; brother in real life, so I admit I may be biased.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T22:08:16-07:00","id":209829,"title":"","content":"Regarding episode 8, it is kind of refreshing seeing a some villains with a masterplan failing miserably right out of the gate, without loosing credibility as a threat*. And I got the &quot;a bit more Asami&quot; I wanted ^_^<br /> <br /> Also liked Bolin's reaction to a Lava bender, since that is likely a way exotic form of earthbending, seeing as it kind of almost crosses into firebending.<br /> <br /> *In fact, it seems their plans tend to hit a lot of snags. Their escapes from prisons were excellently executed, but Air temple infiltration failed, escape from Republic City had to be done by force when they were discovered sneaking out and now they couldn't get Korra. They are personally skilled and fearsome, but apparently not the kind of mastermind villain who is most of the time flawlessly getting away with stuff until the heroes turn the tables at the very end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 07-27-2014, 01:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T13:17:52-07:00","id":210522,"title":"","content":"I continue to be impressed with how well written this season is compared to all the others. My only point of concern right now is Jenoa's spirit powers from the previous episode. They seem to be a little &quot;deus ex machnia-y&quot; at times.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T16:34:21-07:00","id":211803,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out the unsung heroes of this episode, the two nameless metal bender guard mooks who were competent enough to interrupt his first attempt to create a smoke screen and then subsequently fight him head on (off screen unfortunately, but still) for like 4 minutes. If not for their near named character levels of skill and cunning team anti-avatar would have gotten away with Korra using their magical ninja smoke escape technique.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T14:19:28-07:00","id":216147,"title":"","content":"Unalaq was apparently physically incapable of not screwing people over for his own benefit, but in his defense it really should have set off a few alarms in the Red Lotus when the leader of a government joined a secret society that wanted to eradicate governments so they were basically asking for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:47:01-07:00","id":216218,"title":"","content":"Loved this episode. A lot of good comedy bits, good work on advancing characterization and though there wasn't much action, the little we got was good as pretty much always. The revealed motivation of the villains and the tie to the last season were kinda meh for me. There were some neat things about it, but overall I was not too fond of it. Can't seem to articulate why...but in the end it will depend on how it is played out, anyway. Good execution has saved <i>much </i>weaker stuff before and this season has been rather well executed so far. I still think these four might have potential to be the best antagonists on Avatar (including The Last Airbender).<br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Also, I'm surprised that Naga does pretty well in such an arid climate. Speaking of Naga, I really got a kick out of some of the animal antics in this one. Specially Naga nudging Korra because she wants a treat (and looking more like a bump than a nudge because Naga is huge) and Pabu playing with the pair of cute spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 08-01-2014, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T22:47:20-07:00","id":216496,"title":"","content":"I have to admit I'm pretty disappointed with Zaheer's motive. &quot;Reduce the world to chaos&quot;? Really? He's just a glorified anarchist now. Still an awesome character, even if his motives are lame. I wonder how much of what he said was true, and how much of it was just bullshit to distract Korra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T02:15:34-07:00","id":216616,"title":"","content":"I can see why someone would think that bringing about an end to the Four Nations would be a great idea.<br /> Consider the recent history of the Fire Nation and that Sozin's Comet is still a thing and due for a return in less than 30 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T12:26:07-07:00","id":216818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=216616#post216616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see why someone would think that bringing about an end to the Four Nations would be a great idea.<br /> Consider the recent history of the Fire Nation and that Sozin's Comet is still a thing and due for a return in less than 30 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could see that. With only 4 nations in the entire world, villages and cities in each seemingly having a pretty strong national identity and getting pretty xenophobic towards people of the other nations at times, I can see some crazy people thinking things could be improved by tearing down the political system of the entire world by force. Unfortunately, there are a million reasons any reasonable person would see why that wouldn't work. I guess I'm disappointed with the Red Lotus because when Zaheer started to reveal their motives, I wanted it to be something that could credibly give Korra some doubts. As it is, it would feel pretty forced if she saw them as anything other than crazy and/or flat-out monsters.<br /> <br /> I think a more viable idea is demonstrated by Republic City. There were problems in making it happen, sure (some of it can be seen in the Avatar comics). It is not a flawless city, of course. But if the problem becomes &quot;Firebenders with Sozin's comet powers&quot; well, Republic City also has firebenders born there, not members of the fire nation at all. I'd say a wiser person than Zaheer and company would prefer trying to expand the idea of republic city, break down the hegemony of the four nations by creating more and more incentives for these peoples to mingle and, soon enough, they will want a different representation on their own. When your region has a bunch of benders of all types and a culture influenced by aspects of the cultures all those people came from...at some point the people won't accept a Firelord or Earth Queen as their ruler.<br /> <br /> Realistically, there would still be the risk of bloody revolutions, possibly all-out war with that approach. In the real world empires and monarchies, even if led by a good person like Zuko, wouldn't just abandon their power. But still a lot less death and strife than bringing down the entire structure at once by force.<br /> <br /> Then there is the possibility that the end they just want to take the reins of power for themselves, what with the talk of building order from the chaos and stuff. So they probably understand long-lasting anarchy doesn't work. We'll see that they have in mind as a new system instead of the four nations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T16:37:04-07:00","id":223699,"title":"","content":"Good to see Asami still gets to shine every now and then. Also nice to see Zuko again. An entertaining episode, but there were some things that bothered me:<br /> <br /> First, that queen didn't look very young, strange that she apparently didn't have anyone in a line of succession.<br /> <br /> Also, the implication I'm getting that the red lotus plans to bring longstanding anarchy just by killing the current rulers would be such a simplification of how leadership, politics, big organizations and large gatherings of humans in general work as to be stupid, so I hope their plan is not that.<br /> <br /> Finally, while Bolin is clearly the comedy dumb one, his brother is not all that smart either, is he? Why was he trying to sever each individual metal bar with his fire-bending, instead of melting something small that would get them free, such as the lock or the bolts on the door hinges?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T04:47:29-07:00","id":224039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=223699#post223699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good to see Asami still gets to shine every now and then. Also nice to see Zuko again. An entertaining episode, but there were some things that bothered me:<br /> <br /> First, that queen didn't look very young, strange that she apparently didn't have anyone in a line of succession.<br /> <br /> Also, the implication I'm getting that the red lotus plans to bring longstanding anarchy just by killing the current rulers would be such a simplification of how leadership, politics, big organizations and large gatherings of humans in general work as to be stupid, so I hope their plan is not that.<br /> <br /> Finally, while Bolin is clearly the comedy dumb one, his brother is not all that smart either, is he? Why was he trying to sever each individual metal bar with his fire-bending, instead of melting something small that would get them free, such as the lock or the bolts on the door hinges?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, she might not be very young, but she's not exactly a nice person, or very good looking for that matter. I also don't really see her as the motherly type.<br /> <br /> Zaheer also stated that he killed the Earth Queen just to get Korra to come to him, so I doubt that he's that stupid.<br /> <br /> Lastly... Holy shit, Zaheer just choked that woman to death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T05:03:32-07:00","id":224041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mizu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=216147#post216147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unalaq was apparently physically incapable of not screwing people over for his own benefit, but in his defense it really should have set off a few alarms in the Red Lotus when the leader of a government joined a secret society that wanted to eradicate governments so they were basically asking for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well at the time he joined he was second in line to be chief. They probably saw him moving himself into position as heir apparent, removing the loyal prince, to be a coupe for them, he could dissolve the system from the top. By the time he actually was becoming chief... oh look everyone else in the Red Lotus powerful enough to oppose him has just been arrested, &quot;why yes Fire Lord Zuko I will help you contain the dangerous Combusion-Bender... who is also the only possible leverage I can hold over Zaheer's head to keep his mouth shut while I pursue my own agenda.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T05:20:21-07:00","id":224044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=216496#post216496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit I'm pretty disappointed with Zaheer's motive. &quot;Reduce the world to chaos&quot;? Really? He's just a glorified anarchist now. Still an awesome character, even if his motives are lame. I wonder how much of what he said was true, and how much of it was just bullshit to distract Korra?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chaos isn't the goal. Chaos is an instrument and a consequence. The goal is the removal of falsely imposed national borders and the authority of elites. The common people around the world have more in common with each other than they do with the elites of their own countries, and yet the false construct of nations keeps them divided against each other to keep elites in power over them. The goal is to tear down the lie of separate nations and rightful rulership that keeps people chained and blind.<br /> <br /> I mean yes it's &quot;glorified Anarchism&quot; - but you say that like Anarchism isn't a compelling motivation. I mean it's lightyears better than Unalaq's &quot;I will bring about 10,000 years of darkness... BECAUSE BALANCE OR SOMETHING!&quot; covering up a vague inferiority complex/revenge fantasy he's acting out on his cooler big brother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T05:26:18-07:00","id":224047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=223699#post223699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, that queen didn't look very young, strange that she apparently didn't have anyone in a line of succession.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure there are other people who now have a legal claim on the throne - but they're not present/in-control of the Upper Ring when the Red Lotus brought down the walls and called on the people to rise up and take what they want.<br /> <br /> As for a child, she may just have never been able to have kids - or it could be a Queen Elizabeth I situation where marriage would sacrifice her rule by law and tradition to her husband's authority, so she never married and thus no child she could have would be legitimate.<br /> <br /> Of course this is effectively the opposite of Dowager Empress Cixi, the inspiration for the Earth Queen's look, who was an Imperial Consort and then ruled as her son's regent after her husband's death - only to then put some young nephew nominally on the throne when her son died.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:19:59-07:00","id":224355,"title":"","content":"If the ultimate goal of the Red Lotus is anarchy, why do they need Korra? I can't help but get the feeling that Zaheer and his crew have a larger gameplan in mind than just &quot;no leaders ever&quot;. I suspect it might just be a cover for whatever it is they really want to do. Zaheer and Co continue to be very fun villains to watch, regardless.<br /> <br /> On a side note, I was glad that the writing crew actually had the guts to off the Earth Queen the way they did. Brutal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:26:51-07:00","id":224366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=224355#post224355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the ultimate goal of the Red Lotus is anarchy, why do they need Korra? I can't help but get the feeling that Zaheer and his crew have a larger gameplan in mind than just &quot;no leaders ever&quot;. I suspect it might just be a cover for whatever it is they really want to do. Zaheer and Co continue to be very fun villains to watch, regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe Zaheer wants to destroy the Avatar. And I don't mean like, kill her, I mean completely, fundamentally destroy the concept of the Avatar, so Korra will be the last Avatar. The Avatar is, by his or her very nature, a leader, the only person who can unify the four elements. This is pure speculation, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:46:59-07:00","id":224382,"title":"","content":"I hope not, they already butchered the idea of the Avatar in the last two seasons, I would have thought they would have left it alone after that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:01:25-07:00","id":224781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>While My Guitar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=224366#post224366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe Zaheer wants to destroy the Avatar. And I don't mean like, kill her, I mean completely, fundamentally destroy the concept of the Avatar, so Korra will be the last Avatar. The Avatar is, by his or her very nature, a leader, the only person who can unify the four elements. This is pure speculation, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they definitely want her as a tool of some kind. There's definitely more to be learned given that Zaheer refused to answer her last questions in their spirit world encounter.<br /> <br /> Might be cool if they have some plan to go reverse-Amon and open All Bending up to everyone using the Avatar somehow - they won't succeed of course, but that might be an interesting metaphysical goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:03:54-07:00","id":224782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=224781#post224781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be cool if they have some plan to go reverse-Amon and open All Bending up to everyone using the Avatar somehow.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an evil plot that I can get behind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:31:19-07:00","id":224795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JayTee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=224782#post224782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an evil plot that I can get behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Known* among the Exalted fanbase as &quot;pulling a Salina&quot; XD<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">No, not really</span>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:18:18-07:00","id":224836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=224795#post224795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Known* among the Exalted fanbase as &quot;pulling a Salina&quot; XD<br /> <br /> *<span style=\"font-size:10px\">No, not really</span>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Same ideological reason too: trying to destroy power hierarchies (well that's her DotFA motivation, obviously the current writers do not put a ton of stock in Dreams as continuing canon; but it's definitely a more compelling motive than &quot;Sorcery derives from instinct and nature; or I've decided it SHOULD, so I'll cosmically rewrite nature to let people learn Sorcery from it.&quot; which was her philosophy as shown by the Pre-DotFA Sorcery supplements)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T15:27:01-07:00","id":237462,"title":"","content":"Just finished watching the season and all I have to say is damn did that end on a depressing note. But if nothing else I <i>really</i> want Season 4 now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:07:34-07:00","id":237588,"title":"","content":"I wonder if she will actually fully recover from the mercury poisoning...and does anyone knows the title of book four or what it the theme for it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T13:05:38-07:00","id":238440,"title":"","content":"Man, the moment I saw those green crystals I had a flashback to Azula ganking Aang. Avatars and green crystals do not mix.<br /> <br /> EDIT: On a completely unrelated and utterly whacky note, I found <a href=\"http://th07.deviantart.net/fs70/PRE/i/2014/234/4/5/tenzingelion_q___3_33_you_can__not__change_by_steveahn-d7w8ww6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2034,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","user":"JayTee","date":". 08-23-2014, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T18:06:54-07:00","id":238729,"title":"","content":"without posting spoilers:<br /> <br /> i'm left confused with this season, i'm caught between loving it and hating it. It felt EXTREMLY rushed especially the last 2 episodes...and i think the season finale could have benefited by being a two parter.<br /> <br /> <br /> The relationships(romantic and otherwise) kinda just felt...blah. Like they were missing something, but this seems to be the problem in LoK...I found myself not giving a flying fuck what happened to Korra and actually was hoping they'd kill her(oh i knew they wouldn't but eh wishful thinking).<br /> <br /> The bad guys fell flat for me as well. I wanted to turn the TV off when Zahir(or however his name is spelled) started rambling about his &quot;grand plan&quot;. In truth the plan was a great story line and could have been great if it hadn't sucked so bad in its execution. They were THIS close to being an understandable evil, but then went right off the rocks at the end...Though I did find myself agreeing with him in regards to the avatar...so eh. I also wanted more back story on the bad guys, but that may be that i just don't like the whole &quot;I am a bad guy for reasons&quot; shit and prefer fleshed out people you can relate to and maybe even sympathize with.<br /> <br /> Wow just realized while typing I cant really find much I liked about this season. I could go on and on about the crap i hated, or found annoying though lol o0 <br /> <br /> I really enjoyed seeing the scenes involving the air nation, in fact that's a big reason i kept watching i wanted to see how that would turn out. Tenzin, and his kids are interesting to me, more so then the main plot.<br /> <br /> Despite my total lack of interest in the next season I plan to watch it(its kinda like a train wreck...) I do hope perhaps they keep Korra in that chair, could actually make things interesting...but i doubt that'll happen. Who knows MAYBE the final season can redeem this.(I did like season 1 after all)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\"><span style=\"color:#ee82ee\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><i><u>Follow me on twitter! <a href=\"https://twitter.com/scelestai\" target=\"_blank\">https://twitter.com/scelestai</a></u></i></b></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/897-scelesta","name":"Scelesta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"551"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T10:55:15-07:00","id":239340,"title":"","content":"I found Zaheer to be very interesting as a villain: That he used the philosophical teachings of a peaceful people to justify his agenda is a story element I don't come across often. He is the &quot;rogue monk&quot; and makes me think of the Buddhist mobs in South Asia who have been in the news for attacking Muslims. I think the themes of this season have matured and because of that I think this season suffered from constrained episode length - these are good stories that need more time to be told.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"right\"><span style=\"font-size:28px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">\u263e</span></span></b></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/438-wulf","name":"wulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar438_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:35:57-07:00","id":245345,"title":"","content":"So, I only started watching season 3... a bit more than a week ago, I think. And I caught up with it today, because I could hardly keep away from it.<br /> <br /> What can I say other than that, to me, the show has finally made the transition from generally okay to pretty excellent?<br /> <br /> Korra herself feels like she was a much more grounded character in this season, in a manner that I'm satisfied as having emerged naturally from her experiences in the last two, and other characters in general managed to drop most of their annoying traits, allowing me to just enjoy their personalities and dynamics. On top of that, I enjoy the little arcs they all got based more on their interpersonal dramas (and not in the manner of Drama, as in the prior seasons).<br /> <br /> I also enjoyed the driving premise of the series; it was a nice shake up, something with believably deep meaning for some of the characters, and one that gives a chance to explore and expand on something that was never really possible before. I also like how it gave an impetus to return to some old locations, and get a first look at some new ones.<br /> <br /> The villains were also a significant improvement for me. The Equalist concept was a bit overambitious for the length of the season, when it wasn't just a bit lacking in credibility (it's a bit hard to buy the sense of a fundamental inequity between Benders and non-Benders when Mako and Bolin grew up on the streets and Asami lived in a grand mansion), and Vatu and Unaloq were kind of vague and esoteric. Having characters who were a good deal more down to earth really helped enable letting the season have that interpersonal drama I was talking about, and I find the Red Lotus' brand of anarchy a lot more believable as a motive than what the other villains had. I like the characters themselves; I would have liked a bit more development for them, but I think their soft spoken interactions with one another gave them a reasonable level of personality, while also fitting with their context (of being heavily driven and also kind of out of it for a while). Their actual plans were elegant in their simplicity in concept and execution, and they were certainly believably threatening (helped by actually killing somebody for once, and kind of graphically at that, without needing to fixate on it). I can honestly say that I got a stronger sense of tension and danger with them than I've ever gotten with Avatar villains, and it helped make the stakes feel high without having to resort to a &quot;world in danger&quot; plot.<br /> <br /> Zaheer in particular was one who I had doubts about in his first appearance (I was about dubious on the content and acting of his monologue), but I feel he came into his own more when he got to interact with his fellows and with Korra. I also found the concept of him rather fascinating, an &quot;evil&quot; Airbender, not just in his abilities but his enthusiasm for the teachings of an ancient Air Nomad, and applying them to his own situation. In many other cases, I would have felt that the development of the ability to fly was pretty cheap, but setting up how he could do it in his actual character and then triggering it within the context of the scene, it worked very well.<br /> <br /> Personally, I also get a kick out of the idea that there was a splinter group from the White Lotus based on a dispute of their purview changing (literally right before watching the episode where Zaheer explained his background, I'd been thinking again about what a big change they'd had). That and how Ming-Hua gave us another example of using Bending to overcome disability at the same time as producing a distinct and interesting style.<br /> <br /> The whole thing managed to feel very well paced and well constructed to me, tightly focused and held together despite having characters far apart in various cases, and building up coherently to its conclusion.<br /> <br /> It was also nice to see Zuko again, and to open the possibility that we might see Toph in the future.<br /> <br /> And I liked the bittersweet note the season ended on; its sense of consequence was very fitting to the tone and escalation that had been running throughout, and it leaves me enthusiastic to see where they'll go from here. It reminds me of the kind of thing people said they wished the first season ended with, but I find this premise more compelling than inability to use Bending.<br /> <br /> To cap it all off, the action was among the best it's ever been. This season alone skews my whole curve for judging the action across both shows. And like all good action, I really cared about the people and circumstances involved; I bought that and why they were fighting.<br /> <br /> So yes, they really raised the bar with this one. I look forward to the next one with more enthusiasm than ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T11:23:48-07:00","id":245493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=183156#post183156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Korra and Asami have much better chemistry with each other than they do with Mako.</div> </div> </div> </div>I too saw that. I like it!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:00:20-07:00","id":245644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=245493#post245493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I too saw that. I like it!</div> </div> </div> </div>I otherwise share your opinion, but what about the unconventional option ? Threesome Bi Polyamory. No Triangle Drama and No Romantic Frustration. Everyone Benefits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> &lt;Bolin impersonation&gt; The Badass Adorable Amazonian Beauty, the Action-Girl Femme Fatale, and the Brooding Teen with Hidden Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T16:17:31-07:00","id":245692,"title":"","content":"Mostly, I just like female characters to actually have consistent and friendly interactions with one another. You know, the whole Bechdel thing being applied properly.<br /> <br /> I also just think they make for a good double-act; I certainly enjoyed the bit where somebody assumed Asami was the Avatar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T16:54:59-07:00","id":245699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/163188-legend-of-korra-season-3-electric-jamboree?p=245692#post245692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly, I just like female characters to actually have consistent and friendly interactions with one another. You know, the whole Bechdel thing being applied properly.<br /> <br /> I also just think they make for a good double-act; I certainly enjoyed the bit where somebody assumed Asami was the Avatar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I know, and I don't disagree with you. I was simply mocking the excessive importance the Korra fanbase seems to give to romance subplots or their absence in LoK and they causing so much hatedom for Mako. I don't mind either way, but I'm not displeased with some little romance subplot to spice up the main plot or all the family-drama stuff we got last two seasons. It fits with the age of the Krew, and for the same reason it also seems realistic it often gets messy, experimental, filled with melodrama, and poorly communicated. Ironically enough, the lauded first Korra-Asami scene in ep. 1 fails the Bechdel test because they talk about a man, although in that case the restriction should not really apply. But I'm serious about shipping Makorrasami, especially after this season added the Korrasami chemistry for the last side of the triangle. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 08-31-2014, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T12:35:08-07:00","id":246319,"title":"","content":"Man, the new world order channels Miyazaki like crazy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T18:07:14-07:00","id":263287,"title":"","content":"Please disregard this message.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":".  There is no delete button, so I'm just blanking this post. 09-23-2014, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T11:24:41-07:00","id":267538,"title":"","content":"...I loved this season.<br /> <br /> Favorite moment was Zaheer's moment of enlightenment. It's interesting seeing a villain undergo that sort of spiritual epiphany, and I'm a really big fan of Evil Buddhist villain archetypes. It's cool to see that the sort of spiritual journey the Avatar always goes on will also empower regular benders. He's excellent Abyssal or Adorjani Exalted inspiration.<br /> <br /> I also really like this season because it's the first one that feels like it's not living under the first series' shadow. They're doing new things here, changing the world in interesting and permanent ways. They're having conversations about the nature of Power in a more sophisticated way than Aang did. &quot;Killing is bad, so have so much overwhelming power that you can win without having to do so&quot; is a great personal moral dilemma, but Aang's not exactly setting an example that other people can reliably follow. I really like that the show is asking questions like &quot;when is it okay to destroy a corrupt ruler,&quot; and &quot;what is the best way to protect the people from exercises of power by their rulers&quot; and &quot;are all rulers corrupt by nature,&quot; &quot;is a strong ruler necessary to protect people from other strong people, even if that ruler is corrupt?&quot;<br /> <br /> Korra is straight-up okay with killing people, here. They set up villains that I cared about, who obviously had histories and love interests and their own spiritual journeys, and the heroes killed them. Villains who the hero...didn't really disagree with, but just thought their methods of achieving the hero's own goals were too extreme. And it was hard and it was painful, and it did not really solve any of the world's problems.<br /> <br /> Character growth was good, I love Asami and I love seeing the effects of this sort of thing on Korra. Adorable Airbenders were adorable, the art and the fight scenes were consistently gorgeous, and I really enjoyed the fact that the world of the story was permanently changed by their actions rather than just &quot;bad guy beaten, back to normal.&quot; Legend of Korra's not always perfect, and it's still not the original series...but it's better than most of the other stuff I see on TV these days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}